  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "$$\n{{\\{1,2\\}\\cap \\{3\\}=\\{1,2,3\\}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{9\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∧B$ is {{field-3}}.",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is false, and $B$ is false. Therefore, the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{\\{1,2\\}\\cap \\{3\\}=\\{1,2,3\\}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{9\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{false}∧\\text{false}≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
